WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.320
It is
a privilege to be a detective.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.440
Mark Birch: You deal with lots
and lots of horrible things,

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.440
that comes with the territory.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.440
The majority of us
don't have to see these things,

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.480
don't have to
deal with these things.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.040
The launch of the fifth
murder enquiry in such a

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.840
short space of time ...

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.920
Martin Brunning: Justice for
the victims is absolutely

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.160
the most important thing.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.000
- You've been arrested
on suspicion of attempted

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.480
murder and murder.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.040
- Could be worse.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.480
Officer PTC: We can
only imagine the grief of

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:34.360
the families who lost
their loved ones in such

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.720
brutal circumstances.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.000
- ... with your DNA.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.280
How can that be?

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.920
- No comment.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.880
Journalist PTC: The judge
said the murder showed a degree

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.560
of premeditation and planning.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:47.880
He'd been stabbed and beaten.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.200
Howard Groves: It was very much
a manhunt at that stage

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.400
of the investigation.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.320
He knew that the
walls were closing in on him.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.360
Stewart Gull: I always remember
a more experienced officer

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.560
telling me, you know, you,
you never forget these jobs,

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.360
and he was right.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.160
VO: These are the detectives
who solved some of Britain's

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:07.280
most notorious homicides.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.960
Now they re-live those cases.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.640
Martin Brunning: Every fear
that I had was being realised

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.520
in front of my eyes.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.000
VO: Through every twist and
turn of the investigation ...

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.160
Mark Birch: The only way you
forget about it is ...

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.160
is when you're asleep.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.120
VO: Their personal accounts
reveal what it really takes

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.240
to capture a killer
and bring them to justice.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.080
Howard Groves:
As a detective, you know, there,

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.040
there can't be any
greater honour than for you to

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.000
investigate the death - or
murder - of another human being.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:57.520
Stewart PTC: It's often described as a privilege

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.360
to investigate the death of another human.

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:06.920
It's also a significant onerous
responsibility and whilst you

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.640
will always work as
part of a much broader team,

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.600
um, ultimately
the buck stops with you.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.000
Stewart PTC: In 2006 I
was the Head of Crime Services.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.400
I considered myself
to be a fairly experienced and,

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:37.680
er ... confident
leader and investigator.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:42.040
But these circumstances that
we were being presented with,

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:47.880
for me, were unprecedented
and, and unparalleled in living

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:54.000
memory in ... in my county.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.880
VO: In early November,
worried Suffolk mother Kerry

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.880
Nicol reports
her daughter Tania as missing.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.840
Stewart PTC: It wasn't
unusual for Tania to sometimes

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:14.240
stay overnight with friends,
but she hadn't been heard

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.720
of for twenty-four,
forty-eight hours.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:21.400
Mum became a bit more concerned,
she was unable to contact Tania,

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.480
and she, er,
reported her missing.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:30.200
Stewart PTC: We were able
to track her final movements.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:34.960
She caught the bus into town,
and we secured some CCTV

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.600
footage which clearly
showed Tania late on that night.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.120
But from thereon in she
simply disappeared off

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.320
the face of the earth.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.880
VO: Tania was only
nineteen and police

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:55.360
had immediate concerns.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.480
Stewart PTC: There's
something not right here.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:00.160
She had a mobile phone
and we were able to quickly

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:05.360
look at her call records,
which showed standard traffic,

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:08.480
both incoming and outgoing.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.360
But from the 30th of October
you just saw a flat line,

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.880
the phone
had dropped off the network.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.240
VO: There was another
factor that put Tania at risk,

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.360
one that not
even her own mother knew about.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:27.400
Stewart PTC: There
was intelligence and evidence

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.600
to suggest that she was
working as a, a street worker,

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.240
a prostitute.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:37.520
When you look at those
circumstances and the profile

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:43.040
of Tania you're already dealing
with a high risk missing person.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.920
It's important
that we left no stone unturned.

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.360
VO: Early on in
the case one man repeatedly

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.040
makes himself
known to the police.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.200
Stewart PTC:
He was really quite engaging,

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:03.400
quite candid with the officers
and indicated that he knew

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:07.040
Tania, that they'd
been together on a client basis.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:13.760
He would regularly pick up
street workers and prostitutes

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.680
from the Ipswich area.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:18.800
Stewart PTC: He was sort
of putting himself out there

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.120
saying 'You should show
some interest in me,

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:26.040
look at me, I knew Tania,
I'd been with her,

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.760
er, I'm clearly somebody
that you should be, er,

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.000
interested in'.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:33.040
Um, which
was, which was quite unusual.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.480
The surveillance team were
deployed for a couple of days

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.360
during early November -
mainly to assess his lifestyle,

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.760
just to try and build up
a much fuller picture of

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:49.560
the man that was,
um, presenting himself to us.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.160
VO: But the surveillance
of this man produces no useful

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:56.720
leads and police
are no closer to finding Tania.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:00.560
Stewart PTC: With each passing
day of course Tania is missing,

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:01.800
you fear for the worst.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:06.640
You recognise that on the
balance of probabilities Tania

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.000
may well end
up being found dead somewhere.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:17.240
VO: Then fourteen
days after Tania Nicol,

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:21.400
another local woman disappears.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.200
Stewart PTC: Gemma Adams
was reported missing

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.200
by her boyfriend.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:29.040
He'd driven her
into Ipswich, dropped her off,

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:32.800
and they'd agreed a pre-arranged
pick-up time during

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:35.720
the early hours of
the following morning.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:40.080
So the boyfriend had,
had driven back in and had

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:45.200
waited for Gemma to appear
and, um, she didn't return.

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:51.160
Gemma was a prostitute,
she was a street worker,

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.280
she used drugs.

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:58.520
Gemma came from a, a
loving family, very supportive,

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:05.320
she'd probably just taken the
wrong turn early on in her life.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.560
She was a little bit older
than Tania, she was twenty-five,

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:09.560
but they knew one another.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:13.160
Stewart PTC:
Here we are now two weeks later,

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:18.520
still no sign of Tania
and we've got a second young

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:21.800
woman who's gone missing.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:25.720
The concerns are heightened
and raised even further

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:27.800
at this point.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.520
You recognise
the similarities.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:37.560
We quickly assessed
her mobile phone records and it,

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:41.040
it showed a similar
profile to that of Tania.

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:45.320
Lots of activity, incoming
and outgoing calls and texts

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:48.480
up to the point of her disappearance and then

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:49.800
a flat line.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.440
VO: Detectives ramp up the
search for the two missing

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:00.240
women with extensive
local appeals for information.

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:05.160
Stewart PTC: The disappearance
of two young vulnerable

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:08.160
women caused grave concern.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:13.800
We feared for the worst
and we planned for the worst.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:19.040
Stewart PTC: So as the Head of
Crime Management for the Suffolk

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.760
Constabulary it was my ultimate
responsibility to see that

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:27.640
we found these young women.

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:30.160
VO: For over a month
there is little progress.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:34.760
But then comes
a terrible discovery.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.120
Stewart PTC: I was at home
with my wife, it was lunchtime,

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:41.360
my mobile phone rang.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:44.560
Um, and my deputy
told me that, um,

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:48.720
a water bailiff near Belstead, just outside Ipswich,

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:53.800
had found what, er, appeared
to be the naked body of

00:08:53.880 --> 00:09:00.400
a female in the Belstead Brook.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:02.880
News footage: I'm moving
leaves and bracken away,

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:04.640
saw the hair
flowing and the golden earring.

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:09.960
Right on the bend with her
head this end, facing upstream.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:13.200
Suddenly realised that
I'd come across a dead body.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.880
Stewart PTC: Our working
hypothesis was that

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:23.880
this body was one
of our young vulnerable women.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:28.680
Stewart PTC: There'd
been significant flooding,

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:33.080
the terrain was extremely
heavy and muddy and I do recall

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:35.440
we needed the assistance
of a fire and rescue service

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:40.280
to actually retrieve
a body from the Belstead Brook.

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:42.280
You're automatically
thinking about forensic

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:45.920
opportunities, but of course I'm
already aware that she's naked,

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:51.000
she's in fresh water,
which is highly destructive.

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:55.000
So the potential
for the recovery of any forensic

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:59.400
evidence was, was
going to be ... very limited.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:01.560
If, if not impossible.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:07.320
Stewart PTC: The fact
that she was naked,

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:10.600
you automatically think
was there a sexual motive

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:14.280
to this untimely
death of this young woman?

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:18.280
Was the murderer,
in removing her clothing,

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.520
did he or she or they
think about that they were,

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:26.160
er, potentially
eliminating forensic evidence?

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:31.080
VO: Following a post-mortem
police put a name to the victim.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:34.960
Stewart PTC: Within a short
period of time we were able

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.480
to establish it was Gemma.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:43.360
The pathologist was unable
to determine a cause of death

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:47.120
at that stage, but certainly
confirmed in our minds that

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:51.040
we were now dealing with a,
you know, er, case of homicide.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:57.520
Stewart PTC: We confirmed
that this was Gemma

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:02.720
so the prospects
for Tania weren't looking good.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:06.120
VO: Specialist divers from
Norfolk Police are called in

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:08.560
to help search Belstead Brook.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:11.520
For nearly a week
police comb the freezing waters,

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:13.840
hunting for anything
that might throw light

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:15.240
on Gemma Adams's death.

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:20.240
Stewart PTC: The soil was
heavily sodden so it was

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.400
really quite challenging.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:24.880
But of course we wondered
where Gemma's clothes were and,

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:28.520
and it wasn't inconceivable
that we may have found them

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:30.720
somewhere within
the Belstead Brook.

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:36.960
VO: Six days later,
two miles downstream,

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.880
they find something
else entirely.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:45.200
Stewart PTC: I do remember
distinctly getting a call to

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:49.080
say that the same dive-and-wade
team had come across a,

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:52.840
a body further
along the Belstead Brook,

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:59.720
and that was
believed to be Tania.

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:03.640
VO: In Suffolk,
the search for two missing

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:06.680
young women has become
a double murder enquiry with

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:09.680
the discovery of two bodies
in a brook near Ipswich.

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:13.520
Leading the investigation
is Detective Stewart Gull:.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:17.720
Stewart PTC: It wasn't eve
on my radar that I thought

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:21.400
that we'd find Tania in
the same body of water as Gemma.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:26.680
News footage: My initial
reaction was one of complete

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:28.080
and utter disbelief.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.520
Your mind goes into
a bit of a whirlwind.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.240
What's happening here?

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:35.560
How has this happened?

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:38.440
Tania Nicol - she too was naked.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:42.200
We know that she'd been missing
for two weeks longer than Gemma.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:48.640
Assuming she'd entered the water
at the end of October/early

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:52.200
November she'd been in
this water for, for much longer.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:58.960
Stewart PTC: There was no
obvious injury to either Gemma

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:02.920
or Tania and the pathologist
was unable to give us

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.160
any cause of death.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:09.200
What he did note was that, er,
both victims had hyper-inflated

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:13.160
lungs ...
which may have indicated, um,

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:18.760
some form of
interference with the airways.

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:21.040
VO: Determining how
the women died is not

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:24.440
the only difficulty police face.

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:28.320
Stewart PTC: We had nothing
other than two naked bodies.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:30.160
Stewart PTC: We'd already
been investigating Tania's

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:35.840
disappearance for five weeks and
Gemma's for a little over two,

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:40.200
and we'd recovered
little or no evidence.

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:42.480
This increases the challenge,
the professional challenge

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:47.280
to finding those responsible.

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:49.760
Stewart PTC: Were we
looking for the same person

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:50.840
or persons here?

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:54.000
We didn't know at this stage
but the similarities were,

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:58.000
you know, were striking.

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:01.040
VO: As detectives struggle
with the lack of trace evidence,

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:03.520
news of the young women's
deaths is sending shock

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:06.520
waves across the county.

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:09.080
Stewart PTC: Suffolk is
one of the safest places

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.360
to live in the UK.

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:15.480
We would experience on
average somewhere between six

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:20.760
and seven murder investigations
during the course of the year.

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:24.200
Incidents of this
nature are very rare.

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:29.440
Certainly unprecedented
in living memory as far

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:33.440
as Suffolk was concerned.

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:35.720
VO: Street workers in
Ipswich red light district

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:37.840
are particularly anxious.

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:40.920
And particularly at risk.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.680
Reporter: Why have you
decided to come out tonight?

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.080
'Cause I need the money.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:45.520
I need the money.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:47.600
You know.

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:48.920
Despite the dangers?

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:52.640
Well ... it has made me a bit
wary about getting into cars,

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:54.800
you know.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:57.120
But presumably you,
you will do that tonight?

00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:02.800
Woman: Well, probably.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:04.680
VO: Then just two days
after Tania there's

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:06.080
another shocking find.

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:12.560
Stewart PTC: I was ironing
my shirts for the forthcoming

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:15.680
week and the phone rang and
it was the Force Control Room.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:19.520
Stewart PTC: They told me
a motorist had driven through

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:23.640
the village of Nacton, which
is just to the south of Ipswich,

00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:27.320
and the driver had seen what
initially they had thought was

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:31.960
a mannequin lying in a wooded
area, er, just off the road.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:35.600
But on closer examination
they realised that this was

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:41.040
the naked body of a female.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:49.760
Stewart PTC: We weren't
looking for anybody else,

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:56.520
who on earth is this latest,
er, victim that's been found?

00:15:56.600 --> 00:16:01.840
I think that was probably
one of the lowest moments

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:06.120
in my sort of professional
life because you

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:10.800
just begin to think 'Good grief, what on earth is going on here?'

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:13.240
VO: At first there's little
to connect the bodies found

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:16.480
in the Belstead Brook with
the new discovery at Nacton.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.000
Stewart PTC:
She wasn't found in water,

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:21.400
unlike Gemma and Tania.

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:25.080
She was on dry land.

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:28.360
Stewart PTC: She appeared
to have been laid out in

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:30.560
a cruciform position.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:34.920
She had long peroxide blonde
hair that was drawn back

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:36.480
in a conical form.

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:40.920
Whoever had taken her to this
place appeared to have spent

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:44.400
some time with her, you
know, she wasn't just dumped.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:48.280
Stewart PTC: She
was some distance from the road,

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:49.960
twenty or thirty metres.

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:54.160
The murderer - he or she
- certainly hadn't gone to

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:59.040
any lengths to cover her
up or bury her, disguise her in,

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:03.280
in undergrowth
so it was a little odd.

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:07.760
She had some quite distinctive
tattoos on her upper arm.

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:11.920
Those tattoos
provided us with a name.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:18.720
And the name
was Anneli Alderton.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:21.440
VO: With the light fading
Detective Gull has to make

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:24.680
a difficult decision.

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:27.080
Stewart PTC: You only
get one go at a crime scene.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:30.880
Once you walk away, it's gone.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:35.040
It was now dark, wet and windy
so we wanted to lift her in

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:39.320
daylight in order to maximise
the potential for the recovery

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:41.480
of any forensic evidence.

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:44.440
We agreed that we would leave
her laying there overnight.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:49.600
That was ... a really difficult
decision because of course,

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:52.680
having established her identity,
we needed to tell her family

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:55.080
that that's
what we was going to, to do.

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:59.240
And I suspect her family
probably got little sleep that

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:03.880
night knowing that their loved
one was laying where she was.

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:05.520
But that was
the right thing to do.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:10.600
VO: Details emerge more
clearly connecting 24-year-old

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.960
Anneli with the
first two victims.

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:22.000
Stewart PTC: Anneli had
a similar profile to

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:25.560
that of Tania and Gemma.

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:29.640
She was young,
she had been a street worker,

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:33.520
a prostitute on and off.

00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:37.200
There was some intelligence
to indicate that she had

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:42.120
or was using illicit
drugs so a very young

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.600
and vulnerable female.

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:52.400
Stewart PTC: We used
Doctor Nat Cary, the same home,

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:55.320
Home Office pathologist
and I think it was for

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:58.360
the first time with
this victim he was able

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:01.360
to establish a,
a cause of death.

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:06.000
There'd been some form of
interference of, er, her airway.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:10.880
She also had hyper-inflated
lungs so very similar to

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:18.920
the condition that, er,
Gemma and Tania had been found.

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:19.560
Newsreader: Good afternoon.

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:21.760
Police are investigating
the possibility that a serial

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:23.760
killer could be at large
in Ipswich following

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:26.000
the discovery of
the body of a third prostitute

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:27.760
on the outskirts of the city.

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:33.080
Stewart PCT And it began
to feel like a crime in action.

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:37.160
It's a term that
we use ordinarily just for, er,

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:43.200
kidnaps or demands where
the crime is actually happening.

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:47.000
It means you need to respond
with some speed otherwise

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.440
somebody's going to get harmed.

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:54.760
And of course in these
circumstances we feared that

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:56.360
there may be further victims.

00:19:56.400 --> 00:20:00.240
VO: Racing against
time to prevent another murder,

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:03.080
Stewart's
team is stretched to capacity.

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:06.600
Stewart PTC: Suffolk is
one of the smallest forces

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:09.000
in England and Wales.

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:15.240
In terms of resources
and specialists ... we were

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:16.640
beginning to be stretched.

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:19.040
We were at close
to tipping point.

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:22.240
Support from our immediate
neighbours in Norfolk

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:25.640
and Cambridgeshire
was offered and we accepted.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:27.240
It very quickly escalated.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:30.960
A total of additional three
hundred officers and staff

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.280
who came to our support.

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:37.040
VO: For the police,
the pressure is being felt

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:38.360
from all directions.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.320
Stewart PTC: This
was no longer a local story.

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:45.360
We had media organisations right
from around the world reporting

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:46.920
and following the events.

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:51.280
I can recall the media
saying 'Is the murderer

00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:52.080
toying with you?

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:53.080
Is he playing with you?'

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:57.160
Er, these three victims
were only a stone's throw form,

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:00.440
a few miles from
Suffolk Police Headquarters.

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:03.840
VO: New developments mean
that pressure is only

00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:04.920
going to increase.

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:08.640
Stewart PTC: Following the
discovery of Anneli Alderton,

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:14.080
we quickly become aware that
during the following

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:18.000
twenty-four hours, er,
two other, er, young women,

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:23.160
er, of a similar profile to
the first three are reported

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:24.080
as missing.

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:29.440
And they're Paula
Clennell and Annette Nicholls.

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:31.320
Stewart PTC: So we knew
the clock was ticking

00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:33.360
and it was ticking quickly.

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.360
In Suffolk, Detective Stewart Gull: is leading a

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.400
major murder enquiry.

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:42.400
The killer
is targeting street workers.

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:46.560
Three bodies have already been
found and now two more young

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:49.320
women are missing.

00:21:49.400 --> 00:21:51.640
Stewart PTC: I can remember
appealing specifically

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:54.880
for these two young
women to make contact with us.

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:57.440
Or anybody who may
have known their whereabouts.

00:21:57.480 --> 00:22:01.120
VO: Police warn women in
Ipswich to stay in for

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:03.160
their own safety.

00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:05.120
News footage: Assistant Chief
Constable Jacqui Cheer Please

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:06.000
stay off the streets.

00:22:06.080 --> 00:22:09.800
If you are out alone at night
you are putting yourself

00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:13.840
in danger at this time.

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:15.160
VO: Fear is
spreading throughout

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:18.000
the wider community too.

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:19.680
Reporter PTC: Everybody
here you talk to has

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:20.680
the same thought.

00:22:20.760 --> 00:22:23.160
People are terrified.

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:24.840
Female interviewee: Normally
I ... I'd walk around

00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:26.760
on my own but, um,
at the moment 'cause it's quite,

00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:29.200
it's quite
scary so I've had to get, um,

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:30.920
my boyfriend
to come and meet me today.

00:22:36.360 --> 00:22:39.040
VO: Within twenty-four
hours the fear and shock

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:44.640
consuming Ipswich
reaches a whole new level.

00:22:44.720 --> 00:22:46.160
Stewart Gull:: At 3.05 p.m.

00:22:46.200 --> 00:22:49.760
today police received a call
from a member of the public

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:52.920
who was walking along
the old Felixstowe Road

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:55.080
near the Levington turnoff.

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:58.320
He saw what appeared to
be the naked body of a female,

00:22:58.400 --> 00:23:00.200
about twenty feet off the road.

00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:05.080
Police immediately attended
and have closed the road and

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:07.320
have set up a cordon.

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:09.320
As part of our initial
response the helicopter was

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:14.280
sent up to film the scene.

00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:17.720
Pilot: - Foxtrot-One-Sierra
from Alpha-Nine-Nine.

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:19.960
- Alpha-Nine-Nine go ahead.

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:22.160
- Yeah, unfortunately we've,
looks like we've found

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:24.080
a second body in the woodland.

00:23:24.160 --> 00:23:26.320
Um, it's approximately two
hundred yards and probably

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:29.720
the same distance
in as the first.

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:34.280
Stewart PTC: Within the space
of ten minutes not only have

00:23:34.360 --> 00:23:36.880
we now got a fourth
victim, but we've got a fifth.

00:23:39.440 --> 00:23:44.080
So if there'd been difficult
and dark moments earlier in

00:23:44.120 --> 00:23:48.000
the investigation, goodness only
knows what this place was now.

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:50.800
Stewart Gull: I can confirm
that this afternoon,

00:23:50.880 --> 00:23:54.080
Tuesday December the twelfth,
two bodies have been

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.600
found near Ipswich.

00:23:55.640 --> 00:24:01.240
This is breaking news and we're
giving it to you as we get it.

00:24:01.280 --> 00:24:03.160
Stewart PTC: I'm
not sure who was more aghast,

00:24:03.240 --> 00:24:05.600
the media and
the public or ourselves.

00:24:05.640 --> 00:24:08.400
I thought at one stage
my heart was going to

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:11.120
jump out through the chest.

00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:14.240
VO: The bodies are quickly
identified as those of

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:17.120
the women reported
missing the previous day.

00:24:17.160 --> 00:24:19.520
VO: Annette
Nicholls was twenty-nine.

00:24:19.600 --> 00:24:22.160
She had an 8-year-old child
and she was known as a

00:24:22.240 --> 00:24:25.280
street worker in Ipswich.

00:24:25.360 --> 00:24:30.360
Stewart PTC: Annette
had been laid out in a cruciform

00:24:30.400 --> 00:24:33.720
position, the same as Anneli,
with her hair pulled back.

00:24:33.800 --> 00:24:37.240
VO: The other body found at
Levington is confirmed as that

00:24:37.280 --> 00:24:39.280
of 24-year-old Paula Clennell.

00:24:39.360 --> 00:24:42.920
The way her body had been
left is altogether different.

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:48.320
Stewart PTC: Paula had just
been dumped, just crumpled.

00:24:48.360 --> 00:24:51.560
She literally had just been sort
of tossed into the undergrowth.

00:24:51.640 --> 00:24:56.200
Probably because when
the murderer deposited her there

00:24:56.280 --> 00:24:58.560
police colleagues were
already on the scene in

00:24:58.600 --> 00:25:01.320
Nacton at Anneli
Alderton's find.

00:25:01.400 --> 00:25:05.880
Stewart PTC:
And I think he, she,

00:25:05.960 --> 00:25:09.880
they decided that they couldn't
spend the time that perhaps they

00:25:09.960 --> 00:25:12.960
had with Anneli and Annette,
and that's why Paula was

00:25:13.040 --> 00:25:14.680
just dumped in
the way that she was.

00:25:14.760 --> 00:25:19.280
VO: Investigations into
Paula's last known movements

00:25:19.360 --> 00:25:23.480
bring a chilling realisation.

00:25:23.520 --> 00:25:25.360
Stewart PTC: The media,
understandably as part of their

00:25:25.440 --> 00:25:30.080
reporting and their story,
looked to speak with a number

00:25:30.160 --> 00:25:31.520
of street workers and,
er, one of those who was, er,

00:25:31.560 --> 00:25:35.560
interviewed was ... was Paula.

00:25:35.600 --> 00:25:37.320
Reporter: Woman: Why have
you decided to come out tonight?

00:25:37.400 --> 00:25:38.920
'Cause I need the money.

00:25:39.000 --> 00:25:42.520
Stewart PTC: And she of course
recognised the vulnerability

00:25:42.600 --> 00:25:45.560
and the danger
in what she did.

00:25:45.640 --> 00:25:48.680
She also articulated that she
didn't feel she had a choice.

00:25:48.720 --> 00:25:53.520
VO: Paula had been interviewed
about a killer on the loose

00:25:53.600 --> 00:25:56.880
and days later
she had become a victim herself.

00:25:56.920 --> 00:26:01.960
Stewart PTC: The
post-mortems of both Paula

00:26:04.840 --> 00:26:07.960
and Annette were subsequently
undertaken by the same

00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:11.840
pathologist, and again
he was able to establish a,

00:26:11.920 --> 00:26:15.520
a similar cause
of death to that of Anneli.

00:26:15.600 --> 00:26:17.720
An interference
of the, the airways,

00:26:17.800 --> 00:26:20.440
of some form of strangulation.

00:26:20.480 --> 00:26:24.320
Um, and they too had
hyper-inflated lungs so that

00:26:24.400 --> 00:26:28.320
was now the consistent
sort of presenting factor,

00:26:28.360 --> 00:26:35.560
er, in terms of, in terms
of all five deceased victims.

00:26:35.640 --> 00:26:38.360
VO: Five women with shared
backgrounds in life are now

00:26:38.440 --> 00:26:40.960
connected in death.

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:44.000
Reporter: It is inconceivable
surely that these five murders

00:26:44.040 --> 00:26:46.200
are not the work of one man.

00:26:46.240 --> 00:26:49.480
So Suffolk Police, one of
Britain's smallest rural forces,

00:26:49.560 --> 00:26:51.840
is now dealing with one
of the country's biggest

00:26:51.920 --> 00:26:53.360
serial murder hunts.

00:26:53.440 --> 00:26:57.000
Stewart PTC: With every
additional victim it just

00:26:57.080 --> 00:27:00.560
adds another level of
severity, complexity, challenge.

00:27:00.640 --> 00:27:03.600
All five victims were
found during the course

00:27:03.680 --> 00:27:06.160
of a ten-day period.

00:27:06.240 --> 00:27:07.760
We've got a serial
killer on the loose.

00:27:07.840 --> 00:27:14.000
It really provided for
a focus and an internal

00:27:14.040 --> 00:27:17.800
pressure on needing to
find the individual or

00:27:17.840 --> 00:27:19.840
individuals as
quickly as possible.

00:27:19.920 --> 00:27:21.400
Fiona Bruce: Whoever's
responsible - is still

00:27:21.440 --> 00:27:22.520
out there.

00:27:22.600 --> 00:27:25.520
He's left precious few clues as
to his identity and the police

00:27:25.600 --> 00:27:27.240
desperately need a breakthrough.

00:27:27.280 --> 00:27:30.320
Stewart PTC: There was
a tremendous response from the

00:27:30.400 --> 00:27:35.000
public and the local community,
certainly as things escalated

00:27:35.080 --> 00:27:40.400
that week following the
discovery of Paula and Annette.

00:27:40.480 --> 00:27:41.160
Stewart PTC:
Whilst that's great,

00:27:41.200 --> 00:27:44.200
of course logistically
that presents a, er,

00:27:44.280 --> 00:27:46.320
as a challenge to you.

00:27:46.360 --> 00:27:51.200
Was there a golden nugget in
amongst the information that you

00:27:51.240 --> 00:27:53.160
get form the public?

00:27:53.200 --> 00:27:58.040
We needed a, a huge team
just to be able to manage that.

00:27:58.080 --> 00:28:01.280
The overall challenge
was just the sheer pace,

00:28:01.320 --> 00:28:03.080
the sheer sort of breadth
and depth of what we

00:28:03.160 --> 00:28:03.760
were dealing with.

00:28:03.840 --> 00:28:06.360
Jon Snow: Five women
found dead in the last ten days.

00:28:06.440 --> 00:28:08.640
The hunt for the killer
has become the biggest murder

00:28:08.720 --> 00:28:12.320
investigation ever carried
out by East Anglian Police

00:28:12.400 --> 00:28:14.080
of any county.

00:28:14.160 --> 00:28:17.840
VO: Despite the huge police
investigation there is still

00:28:17.920 --> 00:28:21.840
no key to solving the murders.

00:28:21.920 --> 00:28:27.120
VO: The only suspect
detectives have is the man who

00:28:27.200 --> 00:28:32.200
put himself in the frame right
at the start of the enquiry.

00:28:32.240 --> 00:28:35.680
Stewart PTC: He said 'Well
if I was you, I'd suspect me'.

00:28:35.720 --> 00:28:39.760
He was really
quite a strange individual.

00:28:39.840 --> 00:28:43.200
VO: Once more police
put him under surveillance.

00:28:43.280 --> 00:28:44.600
Stewart PTC:
I can remember, er, getting

00:28:44.680 --> 00:28:47.240
a call late one evening
from the ground command to

00:28:47.320 --> 00:28:49.080
say 'We're behind him.

00:28:49.160 --> 00:28:51.440
He's just picked up a street
worker and he's driving

00:28:51.520 --> 00:28:54.480
out of Ipswich,
what do you want us to do?'

00:28:54.560 --> 00:28:56.200
Put yourself in my shoes.

00:28:56.240 --> 00:28:57.200
What would you do?

00:28:59.960 --> 00:29:02.160
We already
had a number of homicides,

00:29:02.240 --> 00:29:04.440
was this
the potential for another one?

00:29:04.520 --> 00:29:09.360
Of course it was.

00:29:09.440 --> 00:29:11.360
We had some drugs
intelligence and we used that

00:29:11.440 --> 00:29:16.720
as a ruse to stop
him and separate both parties.

00:29:16.800 --> 00:29:20.080
Ultimately to protect her.

00:29:20.120 --> 00:29:22.640
VO: The little evidence
available so far has been

00:29:22.720 --> 00:29:25.120
purely circumstantial.

00:29:25.160 --> 00:29:30.560
But now the Forensic Science
Services drops a bombshell.

00:29:30.600 --> 00:29:33.240
Stewart PTC: I was actually
grabbing a bite to eat, um,

00:29:33.320 --> 00:29:35.640
it was about seven o'clock
in the evening in the canteen,

00:29:35.680 --> 00:29:36.720
I was with my deputy.

00:29:36.800 --> 00:29:40.040
And I can remember
the scientific services' manager

00:29:40.120 --> 00:29:43.120
David Stagg walking up
to me and saying 'Stewart, er,

00:29:43.200 --> 00:29:46.160
I've got some information that I
think you'll be interested in'.

00:29:46.240 --> 00:29:51.000
And it transpired that from all
three of the victims that were

00:29:51.080 --> 00:29:57.200
found on the land - so Anneli,
Paula and Annette - that a DNA

00:29:57.280 --> 00:30:01.880
profile had been recovered
from all three victims.

00:30:01.960 --> 00:30:04.120
And it was the same person.

00:30:04.200 --> 00:30:06.480
And I can remember David
saying to me 'Well don't

00:30:06.560 --> 00:30:08.840
you want to
know who it is?'

00:30:08.880 --> 00:30:11.560
He said,
'It's Steve Wright'.

00:30:11.640 --> 00:30:14.560
So a man by
the name of Steve Wright.

00:30:14.640 --> 00:30:18.040
I think I said
'Who the hell is Steve Wright?'

00:30:18.080 --> 00:30:19.480
VO: Police
are hunting for the killer

00:30:19.560 --> 00:30:23.000
or killers
of five women in Suffolk.

00:30:23.080 --> 00:30:25.560
Three of their bodies have
revealed compelling DNA

00:30:25.640 --> 00:30:28.760
evidence pointing
to local man Steve Wright.

00:30:28.840 --> 00:30:32.440
Stewart PTC: We had his
profile on all three victims

00:30:32.520 --> 00:30:36.240
so this was a most significant,
er, breakthrough in terms

00:30:36.320 --> 00:30:37.200
of the investigation.

00:30:37.240 --> 00:30:42.360
VO: Detective Gull has
to make a high risk call-

00:30:42.440 --> 00:30:44.960
whether to arrest
Steve Wright now, or wait.

00:30:45.040 --> 00:30:48.720
Stewart PTC: We were confident that he was Involved,

00:30:48.800 --> 00:30:52.440
but was he primarily Involved
or was he just an accomplice?

00:30:52.480 --> 00:30:55.520
And that's why we took the
decision to arrest him 48 hours

00:30:55.600 --> 00:30:58.280
later, put him under
surveillance in the intervening

00:30:58.320 --> 00:31:01.880
period to allow us to do
the necessary planning before we

00:31:01.960 --> 00:31:03.760
went and knocked on his door.

00:31:03.840 --> 00:31:05.880
It was
still a big decision to make,

00:31:05.960 --> 00:31:09.160
not to go and
arrest Steve Wright immediately.

00:31:11.240 --> 00:31:16.040
The risk of allowing him further
freedom was probably as high as

00:31:16.080 --> 00:31:19.320
it could be, but
we didn't feel we were ready,

00:31:19.400 --> 00:31:22.640
we needed a little bit more time
to plan for his arrest and learn

00:31:22.680 --> 00:31:25.600
as much about him as we could.

00:31:25.680 --> 00:31:29.400
VO: The DNA evidence only
linked Steve Wright to the three

00:31:29.480 --> 00:31:32.800
women found on dry land,
so the team's original

00:31:32.880 --> 00:31:35.920
suspect remains
of significant interest.

00:31:35.960 --> 00:31:38.560
Stewart PTC:
We couldn't just ignore him.

00:31:38.640 --> 00:31:42.360
We didn't know at that stage
whether in fact Wright

00:31:42.400 --> 00:31:45.120
and this man weren't
working together as a team.

00:31:45.200 --> 00:31:50.200
VO: Police arrest
their first male suspect

00:31:53.680 --> 00:31:54.760
on suspicion of murder.

00:31:54.840 --> 00:31:58.520
While he's questioned
detectives build a profile

00:31:58.600 --> 00:32:00.920
of their newest suspect,
Steve Wright.

00:32:01.000 --> 00:32:04.840
Stewart PTC: We established
that he lived on London Road

00:32:04.920 --> 00:32:08.920
in the heart of the
red light district in Ipswich.

00:32:08.960 --> 00:32:11.040
He appeared to have a partner.

00:32:11.120 --> 00:32:15.640
She was always
working nights in a call centre.

00:32:15.720 --> 00:32:19.760
He worked at a foundry
as a fork-lift truck driver

00:32:19.800 --> 00:32:23.720
He'd been stop-checked on
a couple of occasions in respect

00:32:23.800 --> 00:32:26.880
to both Tania's
and Gemma's disappearance.

00:32:26.960 --> 00:32:30.080
He'd been subject
to house-to-house enquiries.

00:32:30.160 --> 00:32:34.160
We'd got a questionnaire that
he'd completed and interestingly

00:32:34.240 --> 00:32:37.040
we were able to establish
that he'd, he'd lied to us,

00:32:37.120 --> 00:32:38.720
he'd lied to us through
the questionnaire

00:32:38.800 --> 00:32:41.600
and on the road-check.

00:32:41.680 --> 00:32:44.600
VO: Police attention would not
have been drawn to 48-year-old

00:32:44.680 --> 00:32:47.840
Wright if it hadn't been
for a minor crime in his past.

00:32:47.920 --> 00:32:53.160
Stewart We had dealt
with Steve Wright back in 2001.

00:32:53.200 --> 00:32:57.920
He was employed as a
barman in a hotel at Felixstowe.

00:32:58.000 --> 00:33:02.400
He'd stolen some cash from
the till and as we do with all

00:33:02.480 --> 00:33:05.480
individuals who are charged
with offences of this nature,

00:33:05.560 --> 00:33:08.320
we secure a DNA profile.

00:33:08.400 --> 00:33:12.360
So Steve Wright's profile
was already on the national

00:33:12.440 --> 00:33:13.560
DNA database.

00:33:13.640 --> 00:33:17.000
VO: What the DNA evidence
doesn't provide is proof

00:33:17.080 --> 00:33:19.960
of Wright's
Involvement in all five murders.

00:33:20.040 --> 00:33:23.400
The team
hone in on his recent movements.

00:33:23.440 --> 00:33:27.640
Stewart PTC: His vehicle
had been captured on ANPR -

00:33:27.720 --> 00:33:31.040
Automatic Number Plate
Recognition - driving out of

00:33:31.080 --> 00:33:35.240
Ipswich on the nights of
the disappearance of both

00:33:35.280 --> 00:33:38.080
Tania and Anneli.

00:33:38.120 --> 00:33:44.480
Not only have we got these, er,
his DNA on the three victims,

00:33:44.520 --> 00:33:47.200
but we've also got these
other elements now that

00:33:47.280 --> 00:33:56.640
increasingly make
him as our number one suspect.

00:33:59.240 --> 00:34:01.440
Stewart Gull:: A
48-year-old man was arrested

00:34:01.520 --> 00:34:04.000
at his home address in Ipswich
at approximately

00:34:04.040 --> 00:34:05.840
five a.m. this morning.

00:34:05.880 --> 00:34:08.240
He has been arrested on
suspicion of murdering

00:34:08.280 --> 00:34:11.440
all five women.

00:34:11.480 --> 00:34:13.680
Stewart PTC: At the point of
arrest he had a big wobble

00:34:13.720 --> 00:34:16.920
and he virtually collapsed.

00:34:16.960 --> 00:34:22.520
Because he knows,
um, his game is up.

00:34:22.560 --> 00:34:26.040
VO: In custody, however,
Steve Wright gives little away.

00:34:26.120 --> 00:34:29.400
Stewart PTC: Throughout his
detention pretty unemotional,

00:34:29.440 --> 00:34:32.960
pretty detached,
maybe a bit arrogant.

00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:35.920
Officer: This is your earliest
opportunity to give an account

00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:41.680
and that is significant
'cause it makes a difference.

00:34:41.760 --> 00:34:45.520
We've got the last girl to
go missing with your DNA

00:34:45.600 --> 00:34:51.240
and the one before with your
DNA both on their naked bodies.

00:34:51.320 --> 00:34:55.240
How can that be?

00:34:55.320 --> 00:34:58.480
Wright: No comment.

00:34:58.560 --> 00:35:01.160
VO: Throughout eight hours
of questioning Steve Wright

00:35:01.200 --> 00:35:05.000
simply answers 'No comment'.

00:35:05.040 --> 00:35:07.960
Despite this, the Crown Prosecution Service agree

00:35:08.040 --> 00:35:13.600
there's enough
evidence to progress.

00:35:13.640 --> 00:35:14.960
Newsreader: In the last
few minutes Suffolk Police have

00:35:15.040 --> 00:35:18.080
announced they have charged
a man with the murder of five

00:35:18.120 --> 00:35:19.360
prostitutes in Ipswich.

00:35:19.440 --> 00:35:22.320
He is Steve Wright,
the second man to be arrested.

00:35:22.360 --> 00:35:27.640
VO: Police are satisfied that
their initial suspect is not

00:35:27.720 --> 00:35:32.360
Involved in the murders
and release him without charge.

00:35:32.440 --> 00:35:35.920
Steve Wright's trial date
is then set for January 2008,

00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:38.440
a full year ahead.

00:35:38.520 --> 00:35:40.720
Stewart PTC: I think there's
a perception that as soon as

00:35:40.800 --> 00:35:42.720
you've made an arrest,
and certainly charged,

00:35:42.800 --> 00:35:44.120
you've got your man.

00:35:44.200 --> 00:35:45.880
Job done.

00:35:45.960 --> 00:35:49.360
But as I tell all my teams,
that's when the hard work begins

00:35:49.440 --> 00:35:52.480
because we now have
responsibility for building

00:35:52.520 --> 00:35:54.200
a successful prosecution case.

00:35:54.280 --> 00:36:00.280
Nobody else is going
to do it, it's going to be us.

00:36:00.320 --> 00:36:04.440
News footage: We forensically
dismantled Steve Wright's house.

00:36:04.520 --> 00:36:09.800
We took away a lot
of clothing, took away his car.

00:36:09.840 --> 00:36:13.400
On his fluorescent jacket there
were traces of blood from both

00:36:13.480 --> 00:36:17.040
Annette and Paula.

00:36:17.120 --> 00:36:19.520
VO: Wright's Ford Mondeo
also delivers droplets

00:36:19.600 --> 00:36:21.480
of Paula's blood.

00:36:21.520 --> 00:36:24.360
Stewart VO: How on earth
has Paula's blood ended up on

00:36:24.440 --> 00:36:28.040
the back seat of his car?

00:36:28.120 --> 00:36:30.280
VO: But police are still
lacking forensic evidence

00:36:30.320 --> 00:36:36.120
firmly connecting Wright
to Gemma Adams and Tania Nicol.

00:36:36.160 --> 00:36:39.000
Stewart VO: When Tania and
Gemma were recovered from the

00:36:39.080 --> 00:36:42.600
Belstead Brook the chances of
recovering any forensic evidence

00:36:42.680 --> 00:36:44.240
was going to be negligible.

00:36:44.320 --> 00:36:48.840
VO: All the Forensic Science
Service has to work with is

00:36:48.920 --> 00:36:51.160
the women's hair.

00:36:51.240 --> 00:36:55.160
Stewart PTC: They go through
a process of continual washes

00:36:55.240 --> 00:36:59.480
to cleanse the hair, to get rid
of all the debris that

00:36:59.520 --> 00:37:03.280
of course will have gathered
through being in the stream.

00:37:03.320 --> 00:37:06.520
It was somewhere in the region
of two kilos of debris

00:37:06.600 --> 00:37:10.480
that was recovered.

00:37:10.560 --> 00:37:13.320
VO: Within the debris
the forensic team find

00:37:13.360 --> 00:37:16.480
the tiniest but most
crucial fragments of evidence.

00:37:16.560 --> 00:37:21.480
Stewart PTC: From Tania they
recovered just one or two carpet

00:37:21.560 --> 00:37:25.120
fibres that matched the
carpet in the footwell of

00:37:25.200 --> 00:37:27.240
Steve Wright's Ford Mondeo.

00:37:27.320 --> 00:37:33.240
Tania's head at some point
has been in contact with the

00:37:33.280 --> 00:37:35.960
footwell of his car.

00:37:36.040 --> 00:37:39.600
There were fibres recovered from
Gemma's head hair that again

00:37:39.680 --> 00:37:44.440
matched back to
come of Steve Wright's clothing.

00:37:44.520 --> 00:37:48.120
We could demonstrate a
link through fibre transference

00:37:48.200 --> 00:37:49.600
between all five
victims and Wright.

00:37:51.800 --> 00:37:55.040
VO: As the forensic evidence
builds detectives dig deeper

00:37:55.080 --> 00:37:57.680
into Steve Wright's background.

00:37:57.760 --> 00:37:59.760
Stewart PTC: He was a bit of
a Jekyll and Hyde it would seem.

00:37:59.840 --> 00:38:02.240
At face
value quite an ordinary man.

00:38:02.280 --> 00:38:05.000
Steve Wright: There was
certainly a history

00:38:05.080 --> 00:38:07.280
of domestic violence.

00:38:07.320 --> 00:38:10.840
He had a record
of, went back some decades,

00:38:10.920 --> 00:38:12.680
of using prostitutes.

00:38:12.720 --> 00:38:16.440
And he was a regular user
of street workers within the

00:38:16.520 --> 00:38:22.800
Ipswich area.

00:38:22.880 --> 00:38:25.600
VO: Eleven months after
the funerals of Gemma, Tania,

00:38:25.640 --> 00:38:30.040
Anneli, Annette and Paula,
Steve Wright appears at

00:38:30.080 --> 00:38:33.840
Ipswich Crown Court
to be tried for their murders

00:38:38.640 --> 00:38:42.560
Stewart PTC: I think we were
feeling reasonably confident.

00:38:42.640 --> 00:38:44.520
Without being complacent.

00:38:44.560 --> 00:38:48.760
We knew we had a strong case,
but of course until proceedings

00:38:48.840 --> 00:38:52.840
are concluded and the jury
return a verdict you

00:38:52.920 --> 00:38:55.600
can never be sure.

00:38:55.680 --> 00:38:58.520
VO: It takes fifteen days
just to present all the evidence

00:38:58.600 --> 00:39:00.000
against Steve Wright.

00:39:01.440 --> 00:39:03.600
Reporter: Wright admitted
that he had had sex

00:39:03.640 --> 00:39:04.880
with four of his victims.

00:39:04.960 --> 00:39:07.920
But during cross-examination
he claimed it was just a

00:39:08.000 --> 00:39:14.400
coincidence, giving this same
explanation fifty-three times.

00:39:14.480 --> 00:39:17.720
Steve Wright: Stewart PTC: His
broad defence was that he'd been

00:39:17.800 --> 00:39:22.120
with all the victims so yes,
of course you'll find traces

00:39:22.160 --> 00:39:27.880
of my DNA but I'm not
responsible for murdering them.

00:39:27.960 --> 00:39:31.440
VO: After a six-week trial
the jury take just six hours

00:39:31.520 --> 00:39:34.440
to decide their verdict.

00:39:34.520 --> 00:39:37.280
Stewart PTC: The adrenaline
was flowing fairly high,

00:39:37.360 --> 00:39:38.440
the blood pressure was up.

00:39:38.520 --> 00:39:41.440
I'm sure, I think
my hands were shaking

00:39:41.480 --> 00:39:43.040
and my heart was pounding.

00:39:43.080 --> 00:39:46.680
And whilst we thought we had a
strong case we couldn't be sure.

00:39:46.760 --> 00:39:49.880
Trevor Macdonald: The man
on trial for the murder of five

00:39:49.920 --> 00:39:53.640
women who worked as prostitutes
in Ipswich was today found

00:39:53.720 --> 00:39:55.360
Guilty on all counts.

00:39:55.400 --> 00:39:57.760
Kirsty Wark: The serial killer
embarked on one of the most

00:39:57.800 --> 00:40:00.240
intensive killing sprees
in British criminal history.

00:40:00.320 --> 00:40:02.400
News footage: The murders
of these vulnerable young women

00:40:02.440 --> 00:40:05.400
left five families devastated.

00:40:05.440 --> 00:40:09.000
Our sympathies are
clearly with them at this time.

00:40:09.040 --> 00:40:12.280
What I hope is today's Guilty
verdict on their killer brings a

00:40:12.360 --> 00:40:16.680
little comfort to them.

00:40:16.760 --> 00:40:20.280
Stewart PTC: Steve Wright
was very close and personal with

00:40:20.320 --> 00:40:24.840
these young women when they
were at their most vulnerable,

00:40:24.920 --> 00:40:29.240
and maybe it was the fact that
he had life and death in his,

00:40:29.320 --> 00:40:33.800
his hands.

00:40:33.880 --> 00:40:37.440
Stewart PTC: Ultimately the
only man that knows why he did

00:40:37.520 --> 00:40:40.000
what he did is Steve Wright.

00:40:43.680 --> 00:40:47.000
VO: Fifteen months after his
killing spree began Steve Wright

00:40:47.040 --> 00:40:49.640
returns to Court.

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:52.440
Reporter: The man found Guilty
of murdering five young women

00:40:52.480 --> 00:40:55.680
who were working as prostitutes
in Ipswich is to spend the rest

00:40:55.720 --> 00:40:56.920
of his life in prison.

00:40:57.000 --> 00:41:00.280
Steve Wright was told his
carefully planned campaign of

00:41:00.320 --> 00:41:03.560
murder meant that he would
never be eligible for parole.

00:41:03.640 --> 00:41:07.280
Stewart PTC: He
will never come out of custody,

00:41:07.360 --> 00:41:11.240
which I think is,
is right and proper.

00:41:17.440 --> 00:41:19.840
Stewart PTC: The families,
they'll never be able to get

00:41:19.880 --> 00:41:22.600
over the loss of
their loved ones in such tragic

00:41:22.680 --> 00:41:24.080
circumstances.

00:41:24.120 --> 00:41:27.520
But knowing that the man
responsible will never see the

00:41:27.600 --> 00:41:32.240
light of day again hopefully
provides for some solace.

00:41:32.320 --> 00:41:33.520
Isabella Clennell Mother of
Paula Clennell: No parent should

00:41:33.560 --> 00:41:35.960
have to bury their child.

00:41:36.040 --> 00:41:39.760
No parent.

00:41:39.800 --> 00:41:43.200
It was devastating
beyond belief.

00:41:43.240 --> 00:41:46.800
This sort of thing
shouldn't happen to anyone.

00:41:46.880 --> 00:41:50.040
Not just Paula.

00:41:50.120 --> 00:41:52.120
She was helpless,
homeless, penniless.

00:41:52.200 --> 00:41:55.400
The girls
on the street, all five of them,

00:41:55.480 --> 00:41:58.680
had the same sort
of lifestyle and, er,

00:41:58.760 --> 00:42:01.360
people just looked down their
nose at them and ...

00:42:01.440 --> 00:42:04.000
I mean, I used
to ask Paula why did she do it.

00:42:05.680 --> 00:42:08.760
And she would say 'Mum,
because I'm a heroin addict'.

00:42:08.840 --> 00:42:11.960
She was
a fair good lass, lovely girl.

00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:14.400
I miss her dearly.

00:42:20.240 --> 00:42:22.440
Stewart PTC: I can't remember
another case of its nature.

00:42:23.720 --> 00:42:29.440
The scale, the speed,
the magnitude, the coverage,

00:42:29.480 --> 00:42:30.240
the exposure.

00:42:30.280 --> 00:42:33.360
Of course
it's left its indelible mark.

00:42:33.440 --> 00:42:38.080
I found myself in a place
that I never expected to be.

00:42:38.120 --> 00:42:39.520
Hopefully never to be repeated.

